I have written a script that can help if you are satisfied neither with
random pick nor with choosing everything by yourself.  For example you
ascended several creatures and don't want to play them anymore, or you
like playing orcs.  Another feature is that it provides is a possibility
to provide different male and female names, to choose *after* the gender
is picked.  The script is downloadable here:

http://tiny.pl/chhs

You can use it in two ways.  First involves command line:  e.g.

./nhlaunch --yes Orc - gets you a random orc

./nhlaunch --no Pri Val - gets you a character that is neither a priest
nor a Valkyrie

./nhlaunch --yes Kni Cha
./nhlaunch --yes Val Mal - these two display error message

The second one uses a config file.  For your convenience first run:

./nhlaunch -c nhlaunch.conf (or other filename)

Then edit the file the script created putting right female and male name
and turning off some options (turn 1's to 0's).  Then run

./nhlaunch -f nhlaunch.conf

It is not an error to provide both file and --yes or --no parameter.  If
you do it, the arguments will be added/substracted from the list
specified byt the file.

I know, the code can be still buggy, so I appreciate any constructive
comments.  For testing purposes use -t option which will not actually
launch nethack.

